WEBVTT

00:00:40.541 --> 00:00:44.043
FLEX X COP 2

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:46.963
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:48.966
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.095
There's a ghost in the abandoned house.

00:00:54.096 --> 00:00:56.847
I'm sure it's some kind of vengeful ghost.

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:59.475
It's asking us to catch the killer.

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:00.935
- Let's go check it out. - What?

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:02.520
PREVIOUSLY

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:07.985
You check upstairs.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.577
Nutjob!

00:01:17.578 --> 00:01:19.620
Yes, ma'am!

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:21.205
What's going on?

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:23.083
- Hey, what happened? - I don't know.

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:25.418
I got attacked out of nowhere.

00:01:29.965 --> 00:01:32.384
- One... Two, three! - Two, three!

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:45.354
I seriously almost died.

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:47.481
There really is something here.

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:49.442
I have great instincts, huh?

00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:52.445
Let's open it up. There's definitely something in there.

00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:09.378
You were there.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:11.756
I started the fire.

00:02:11.757 --> 00:02:14.217
They might've found something while putting out the fire.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.344
Hyeonsu disappeared.

00:02:16.345 --> 00:02:18.679
Hyeonsu's last location was that house.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.431
You uncovered five bodies?

00:02:20.432 --> 00:02:22.725
Yes, they're performing the autopsy now.

00:02:22.726 --> 00:02:25.061
We performed the autopsy on the most recent victim first.

00:02:25.062 --> 00:02:27.480
The most recently deceased victim

00:02:27.481 --> 00:02:29.024
Had these glasses in their pants.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.108
These belong to Park Hyeonsu.

00:02:31.109 --> 00:02:32.568
Three months ago, at Yuseon-dong...

00:02:33.654 --> 00:02:35.404
...Kim Minseo was murdered.

00:02:35.405 --> 00:02:37.823
Park Hyeonsu's fingerprints were on a knife at the scene.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:41.243
That knife was the knife missing from Park Hyeonsu's house.

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:42.328
MURDER SUSPECT

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:43.537
Wait, so,

00:02:43.538 --> 00:02:46.749
The murder suspect you were after three months ago was murdered

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.752
And his body was found at the abandoned house?

00:02:49.753 --> 00:02:52.546
What if Park Hyeonsu wasn't the one who killed Kim Minseo?

00:02:52.547 --> 00:02:54.048
It's the perfect crime.

00:02:54.049 --> 00:02:55.716
The target.

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:57.843
A victim to frame as the suspect.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:00.137
If they kill the target and the suspect,

00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:01.807
Then make him go missing,

00:03:02.432 --> 00:03:04.309
The case cannot be solved.

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:07.728
Five perfect crimes.

00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:10.107
You need at least two people to make this possible.

00:03:10.774 --> 00:03:12.358
They're methodical and cold.

00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:14.360
So they're professional killers?

00:03:14.361 --> 00:03:16.362
If they came to the house...

00:03:16.363 --> 00:03:18.531
It means they killed someone else.

00:03:18.532 --> 00:03:20.409
They were there to bury the body.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.415
It's blood.

00:03:27.416 --> 00:03:28.666
KILLER 1 JANG JAECHUN

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:29.875
It leaked.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:30.960
KILLER 2 JO BEOMKI

00:03:30.961 --> 00:03:32.170
What do we do?

00:03:32.921 --> 00:03:34.381
Taegwang.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.976
THE KILLER OF KILLERS YU TAEGWANG

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.106
But don't courier deliveries come quickly

00:03:52.107 --> 00:03:54.400
And drop it off at the door?

00:03:54.401 --> 00:03:56.777
They're a bit different from parcel deliveries.

00:03:56.778 --> 00:03:58.154
They usually hand it to you.

00:03:58.155 --> 00:03:59.197
Uh-huh.

00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:03.951
Then the victim must have known a courier was coming.

00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:07.079
Yes, they usually contact ahead.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.582
But this wasn't a real courier.

00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:11.709
So someone must've helped them.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.712
To make her open the door.

00:04:14.713 --> 00:04:16.548
It must be the one she lives with.

00:04:17.424 --> 00:04:18.425
Her husband.

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.469
Who is her husband?

00:04:22.179 --> 00:04:24.848
Nam Jaeguk. He's the CEO of a furniture company.

00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:29.853
IDENTITY RECORD NAM JAEGUK

00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:32.063
Detective Choi, you look into Nam Jaeguk.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.857
And check if Kim Minseo had life insurance.

00:04:34.858 --> 00:04:36.859
- Yes, ma'am. - Detective Park.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.402
You look into the stalking case.

00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:39.612
Understood.

00:04:39.613 --> 00:04:41.031
We'll meet Nam Jaeguk tomorrow.

00:04:41.615 --> 00:04:42.616
Okay.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.418
We're with the police.

00:04:55.212 --> 00:04:56.754
Is Mr. Nam Jaeguk here? :cue

00:04:56.755 --> 00:04:59.340
Yes, what is this about?

00:04:59.341 --> 00:05:02.802
Well, his wife was brutally murdered.

00:05:02.803 --> 00:05:05.054
Do you happen to know anything?

00:05:05.055 --> 00:05:07.557
Like the CEO's secret, for example?

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.018
You think I'd know that?

00:05:11.019 --> 00:05:12.312
Please take us to see him.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.193
EPISODE 4

00:05:19.194 --> 00:05:20.778
Don't go probing just anyone.

00:05:20.779 --> 00:05:22.655
This is an investigation technique.

00:05:22.656 --> 00:05:24.949
Didn't you know? Huh?

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:25.951
Honestly.

00:05:31.206 --> 00:05:33.415
KIM MINSEO'S HUSBAND NAM JAEGUK

00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:34.543
What...

00:05:35.961 --> 00:05:37.295
Is this about?

00:05:38.797 --> 00:05:41.341
We're here about your wife's case.

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.718
You're not the detective in charge.

00:05:44.719 --> 00:05:47.055
We're reinvestigating the case from scratch.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.601
Reinvestigating?

00:05:53.687 --> 00:05:55.105
Park Hyeonsu's the culprit.

00:05:56.523 --> 00:05:57.690
Isn't he?

00:05:57.691 --> 00:06:00.902
Mmm. Someone else might be the culprit.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.780
Couldn't they?

00:06:04.239 --> 00:06:07.284
We heard your wife was being stalked.

00:06:08.285 --> 00:06:09.994
Was the stalker Park Hyeonsu?

00:06:09.995 --> 00:06:11.246
Yes.

00:06:11.872 --> 00:06:13.665
I've already told the police all this.

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:15.749
Don't you share information?

00:06:17.252 --> 00:06:18.837
Please tell us again.

00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:21.922
Did you hear anything about Park Hyeonsu?

00:06:23.508 --> 00:06:25.342
They dated briefly in college,

00:06:25.343 --> 00:06:28.637
Then ran into each other by chance recently.

00:06:28.638 --> 00:06:31.725
After that, he followed her around, trying to get back together.

00:06:33.351 --> 00:06:34.352
That's what she said.

00:06:34.978 --> 00:06:37.771
You mean your wife, Ms. Kim Minseo, said that herself?

00:06:37.772 --> 00:06:40.400
Yes, she did. Why are you bringing this up again now?

00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:42.903
Park Hyeonsu

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:44.696
Has been found.

00:06:49.492 --> 00:06:50.702
How did you find him?

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.999
Mmm, I can't tell you. That's classified information.

00:06:58.001 --> 00:07:00.128
We came to update you on your wife's case.

00:07:01.046 --> 00:07:02.213
We'll be in touch.

00:07:11.556 --> 00:07:13.725
Her husband definitely ordered the murder.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:16.935
How do you know?

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:19.481
"I am guilty" was written all over his face.

00:07:20.148 --> 00:07:21.900
That was pretty much a confession.

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:24.527
There's something else.

00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:27.989
- What? - When we said Park Hyeonsu had been found,

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:30.492
He didn't ask if we'd caught him.

00:07:31.785 --> 00:07:33.203
How did you find him?

00:07:34.162 --> 00:07:35.621
Right, that's true.

00:07:35.622 --> 00:07:38.708
His first concern should've been whether we'd caught the guy.

00:07:39.209 --> 00:07:42.003
- It's because he knows the guy's dead. -  Hmm.

00:07:43.338 --> 00:07:45.382
Hey, take care.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:03.024
Where's my damn phone?

00:08:15.036 --> 00:08:17.955
After today, you mustn't call me, no matter what happens.

00:08:34.973 --> 00:08:37.558
During the month before Ms. Kim Minseo died,

00:08:37.559 --> 00:08:39.477
She filed three stalking reports.

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:42.230
STALKING REPORT

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:45.941
Did you question the suspect?

00:08:45.942 --> 00:08:47.526
No, we weren't able to.

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:48.861
She didn't know who it was.

00:08:48.862 --> 00:08:52.699
She just reported that someone had been following her near her house.

00:08:54.242 --> 00:08:56.452
Ah, for the last report,

00:08:56.453 --> 00:08:59.872
She deliberately caused a fender bender because someone was following her.

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:08.882
10 DAYS BEFORE KIM MINSEO'S DEATH

00:09:13.428 --> 00:09:15.262
Hello, we're responding to a report.

00:09:15.263 --> 00:09:20.142
Yes, I did cause the accident, but I think that man in the car behind me

00:09:20.143 --> 00:09:22.603
Has been stalking me for a few days now.

00:09:22.604 --> 00:09:24.104
That's why I did it.

00:09:24.105 --> 00:09:25.564
What are you talking about?

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:26.566
Hey, lady.

00:09:27.192 --> 00:09:28.817
Why would I follow you around?

00:09:28.818 --> 00:09:30.527
You have. You've been following me.

00:09:30.528 --> 00:09:32.780
Lady, are you crazy? Delusional much?

00:09:32.781 --> 00:09:33.864
But...

00:09:33.865 --> 00:09:35.491
Both of you, please calm down.

00:09:35.492 --> 00:09:37.743
Why would I follow you? Don't be ridiculous.

00:09:37.744 --> 00:09:39.746
IDENTITY RECORD LEE KYUNGSU

00:09:47.587 --> 00:09:50.798
Kyungjin, get a location on this number.

00:09:50.799 --> 00:09:52.591
010-0675-0040. :cue

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:55.969
PARK HYEONSU'S HOUSE

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:57.304
Did you find anything?

00:09:57.305 --> 00:10:00.016
Just some fingerprints and a few strands of hair.

00:10:00.683 --> 00:10:03.103
- Please run them as quickly as possible. - Got it.

00:10:09.567 --> 00:10:10.568
Hey.

00:10:14.572 --> 00:10:16.783
KIM MINSEO 4:00 P.M.

00:10:17.575 --> 00:10:19.827
They met three months before the incident.

00:10:19.828 --> 00:10:20.912
Why did they meet?

00:10:21.579 --> 00:10:22.831
They had no contact before.

00:10:24.332 --> 00:10:25.625
Hmm...

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.651
Found it.

00:10:56.614 --> 00:10:58.825
This is Minseo. It's been a while.

00:10:59.617 --> 00:11:01.077
I hope you've been well.

00:11:02.162 --> 00:11:03.788
I heard you became a lawyer.

00:11:04.664 --> 00:11:06.707
I want to ask your advice on something.

00:11:06.708 --> 00:11:09.626
Could we possibly meet?

00:11:09.627 --> 00:11:11.796
I need your help.

00:11:13.798 --> 00:11:16.092
Kim Minseo was the one who asked to meet first.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.011
Why?

00:11:18.595 --> 00:11:19.596
Because of this?

00:11:26.728 --> 00:11:27.729
Look familiar?

00:11:30.815 --> 00:11:33.483
I don't go around probing people for no reason.

00:11:33.484 --> 00:11:36.153
It's my detective's instinct.

00:11:36.154 --> 00:11:37.322
Understand?

00:11:39.574 --> 00:11:41.034
Mmm-hmm. Mmm.

00:11:53.254 --> 00:11:54.255
Who are you?

00:11:55.798 --> 00:11:56.799
Police.

00:11:58.885 --> 00:12:00.470
I haven't done anything wrong.

00:12:01.346 --> 00:12:03.263
You're parked illegally, for one.

00:12:03.264 --> 00:12:04.557
Am I getting a ticket?

00:12:06.059 --> 00:12:07.435
Did you follow this person?

00:12:11.105 --> 00:12:12.148
Is that your answer?

00:12:12.732 --> 00:12:13.983
Yes, I followed her.

00:12:15.818 --> 00:12:17.278
What about this man?

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:19.989
I took pictures of them meeting.

00:12:21.366 --> 00:12:22.658
Who hired you?

00:12:22.659 --> 00:12:26.704
How would I know that? It's just a part-time gig I do sometimes.

00:12:28.289 --> 00:12:30.332
Besides, I don't work with them anymore.

00:12:30.333 --> 00:12:32.085
Why not?

00:12:33.962 --> 00:12:36.588
That woman died after I took those photos.

00:12:38.299 --> 00:12:39.425
It kept bothering me.

00:12:40.134 --> 00:12:41.677
It felt weird from the start.

00:12:41.678 --> 00:12:44.179
I was told to get proof they were having an affair,

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:46.599
But all they did was drink coffee and talk.

00:12:47.308 --> 00:12:49.018
They didn't even seem close.

00:12:51.604 --> 00:12:54.023
Where was that place you worked?

00:12:55.984 --> 00:12:57.652
I'll start the briefing.

00:12:58.569 --> 00:13:01.655
Nam Jaeguk married Kim Minseo in 2021.

00:13:01.656 --> 00:13:05.033
The furniture company he runs was originally his father-in-law's.

00:13:05.034 --> 00:13:07.161
And Kim Minseo's life insurance payout

00:13:08.121 --> 00:13:09.204
Is one billion won.

00:13:09.205 --> 00:13:11.123
He became a CEO thanks to his in-laws.

00:13:11.124 --> 00:13:14.167
Then killed her for the insurance payout?

00:13:14.168 --> 00:13:15.377
Mm-mm. Mm-mm.

00:13:15.378 --> 00:13:17.213
He's worse than that.

00:13:20.383 --> 00:13:22.551
He even cheated on her.

00:13:22.552 --> 00:13:25.137
With his secretary.

00:13:25.138 --> 00:13:27.140
This is straight out of a soap opera.

00:13:28.266 --> 00:13:30.767
Kim Minseo knew about the affair and wanted a divorce,

00:13:30.768 --> 00:13:33.145
Which is why she met Park Hyeonsu.

00:13:33.146 --> 00:13:37.024
Rather than get fired and end up divorced,

00:13:37.025 --> 00:13:38.776
Nam Jaeguk chose to kill his wife.

00:13:39.319 --> 00:13:42.739
It's clear that Nam Jaeguk was the one who hired someone to kill Kim Minseo.

00:13:43.614 --> 00:13:46.576
The question is, who did he hire?

00:13:47.577 --> 00:13:48.661
There's a PI involved.

00:13:50.872 --> 00:13:52.081
A top PI, apparently. :cue

00:13:54.292 --> 00:13:55.834
What's this?

00:13:55.835 --> 00:13:56.878
A top PI?

00:13:57.670 --> 00:14:00.380
The stalker Kim Minseo reported used to work here.

00:14:00.381 --> 00:14:02.007
All he did was tail her.

00:14:02.008 --> 00:14:03.968
He took photos of her meeting Park Hyeonsu.

00:14:05.553 --> 00:14:07.387
He doesn't look like a top PI.

00:14:07.388 --> 00:14:08.889
He looks kind of dopey.

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:10.725
His name is Myeong Seokho.

00:14:11.392 --> 00:14:12.393
Two fraud convictions.

00:14:13.269 --> 00:14:15.312
Let's go catch that dopey PI!

00:14:15.313 --> 00:14:17.147
Oh. Don't you dare.

00:14:17.148 --> 00:14:18.273
Why not?

00:14:18.274 --> 00:14:20.275
He can just deny it.

00:14:20.276 --> 00:14:22.653
What if he says they were just hired to tail her?

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:25.405
She's right.

00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:26.824
We don't have any evidence.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.787
Myeong Seokho may have planned it, but someone else did the work.

00:14:33.122 --> 00:14:34.999
If we want to catch them...

00:14:37.585 --> 00:14:39.961
We should just hire them ourselves.

00:14:39.962 --> 00:14:41.422
Let's hire them to kill someone.

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:43.173
Right.

00:14:43.174 --> 00:14:45.675
We'll plant a bug, then wait until the hitmen call.

00:14:45.676 --> 00:14:47.511
If we trace it, we'll get their location.

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:50.722
Is this how you normally investigate?

00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:52.767
Hey, it's a trade secret.

00:14:53.518 --> 00:14:56.770
I know it seems a little weird, but it does work.

00:14:56.771 --> 00:14:58.355
You know our track record.

00:15:05.113 --> 00:15:07.906
Come on, we have no evidence. What if they run?

00:15:14.622 --> 00:15:15.790
Fine. Let's try it.

00:15:17.125 --> 00:15:18.126
Okay.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:21.419
Then, shall I pose as the client?

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.463
Mm-mm. You did it last season.

00:15:23.464 --> 00:15:26.551
We need someone who looks like they've got some kind of a past.

00:15:29.345 --> 00:15:30.762
Did any theater as a kid?

00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:32.056
No.

00:15:32.807 --> 00:15:33.890
No.

00:15:33.891 --> 00:15:37.310
My hands start shaking when I'm dealt a decent hand in poker.

00:15:41.566 --> 00:15:43.817
It should be someone older.

00:15:43.818 --> 00:15:46.444
And look like they'd want someone dead.

00:15:46.445 --> 00:15:49.865
Someone with that cold-blooded mobster vibe.

00:15:49.866 --> 00:15:51.742
Does no one fit that bill?

00:15:53.035 --> 00:15:55.204
What are you all doing? Where's my update?

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.336
Oh...

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:04.297
He looks like he could act.

00:16:18.269 --> 00:16:20.270
- Yes, Detective Jin. -  Mr. Choi.

00:16:20.271 --> 00:16:22.397
- I need to borrow your car. - My car?

00:16:22.398 --> 00:16:24.941
Right now. There's no time. Send it to the station.

00:16:24.942 --> 00:16:26.443
What are you...

00:16:26.444 --> 00:16:27.736
We've got hitmen to catch.

00:16:27.737 --> 00:16:29.404
There's a suit in the car, right?

00:16:29.405 --> 00:16:31.656
I need a suit and a watch. Right now.

00:16:37.914 --> 00:16:39.207
Stop the car.

00:16:45.922 --> 00:16:48.382
Another car will be here shortly.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:50.342
I'm sorry, sir.

00:16:50.343 --> 00:16:51.718
Not at all.

00:16:51.719 --> 00:16:53.763
I'm used to this.

00:17:18.162 --> 00:17:19.537
Who is that?

00:17:19.538 --> 00:17:21.414
Did we arrest a mob boss?

00:17:23.501 --> 00:17:24.543
Isn't that Chief Park?

00:17:25.753 --> 00:17:26.754
Gosh...

00:17:28.589 --> 00:17:30.298
What are they doing?

00:17:30.299 --> 00:17:32.176
I have no idea, sir.

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:46.148
There's something wrong with our whole station.

00:17:46.899 --> 00:17:48.526
Good grief. :cue

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:01.162
MYEONG SEOKHO

00:18:07.753 --> 00:18:10.047
It's really taking a nosedive.

00:18:29.734 --> 00:18:30.776
Who are you?

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:56.010
Would you like something to drink?

00:18:58.054 --> 00:18:59.096
Cold brew.

00:19:00.014 --> 00:19:01.015
Decaf.

00:19:02.308 --> 00:19:03.391
Light vanilla.

00:19:03.392 --> 00:19:05.269
Toffee nut latte.

00:19:10.858 --> 00:19:13.444
French pistachio.

00:19:14.362 --> 00:19:15.862
Frappe, served hot.

00:19:15.863 --> 00:19:17.615
- Fra... - Okay.

00:19:18.407 --> 00:19:20.159
I'll go get them right away.

00:19:28.501 --> 00:19:29.502
What in the...

00:19:50.564 --> 00:19:52.525
How can I help you?

00:19:54.735 --> 00:19:56.153
I've got someone to find.

00:19:57.321 --> 00:19:58.322
I heard

00:19:59.198 --> 00:20:00.782
You're good at finding people.

00:20:00.783 --> 00:20:02.618
Oh, yes, well.

00:20:03.327 --> 00:20:06.288
We are the best in the business.

00:20:18.968 --> 00:20:20.261
What did he do?

00:20:21.262 --> 00:20:22.763
He stole...

00:20:24.056 --> 00:20:25.140
My stash.

00:20:25.141 --> 00:20:26.517
What stash?

00:20:30.563 --> 00:20:32.189
What do you think? Foot cream?

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:33.691
Ah.

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:36.944
Ah.

00:20:37.737 --> 00:20:40.196
Then, let's see.

00:20:40.197 --> 00:20:42.783
We'll sign a contract first. Your name is?

00:20:51.876 --> 00:20:53.169
You want to know...

00:20:54.837 --> 00:20:56.130
My name?

00:20:57.673 --> 00:20:59.090
The hell's wrong with you?

00:20:59.091 --> 00:21:00.551
Uh... No.

00:21:03.345 --> 00:21:04.554
No contract necessary.

00:21:07.099 --> 00:21:08.434
I'll find him no matter what.

00:21:18.944 --> 00:21:20.196
Your advance. :cue

00:21:28.329 --> 00:21:29.455
Whoa!

00:21:31.081 --> 00:21:32.541
You have three days.

00:21:34.084 --> 00:21:37.588
If you haven't found him by then...

00:21:43.761 --> 00:21:45.929
Cozy office you've got here.

00:21:48.682 --> 00:21:51.769
Half a can of gas will wipe this place out.

00:21:53.187 --> 00:21:55.146
If you're unlucky,

00:21:55.147 --> 00:21:56.732
Someone might die.

00:22:00.611 --> 00:22:02.446
I won't let you down.

00:22:06.158 --> 00:22:07.534
Let's go.

00:22:07.535 --> 00:22:08.536
Yes, boss.

00:22:11.831 --> 00:22:12.832
That stings.

00:22:18.045 --> 00:22:19.421
Have a good night, sir.

00:22:28.639 --> 00:22:30.723
That was scary.

00:22:30.724 --> 00:22:33.893
Chief, you were amazing. That was convincing as hell.

00:22:33.894 --> 00:22:35.061
You should be an actor.

00:22:35.062 --> 00:22:38.273
I was in the drama club in high school.

00:22:38.274 --> 00:22:39.524
The Drama Lovers Club.

00:22:39.525 --> 00:22:42.444
I knew it. You were a real scumbag.

00:22:43.737 --> 00:22:45.613
That's a compliment, right?

00:22:45.614 --> 00:22:46.698
Let's go.

00:22:46.699 --> 00:22:49.535
Will he buy it, or will he not?

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:52.371
- That is the question. -  Let's go.

00:23:16.353 --> 00:23:17.688
Have a good night, boss.

00:23:18.898 --> 00:23:20.649
-  Thank you, sir. - Right, keep at it.

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:27.864
Hey, any movements?

00:23:27.865 --> 00:23:28.866
No.

00:23:43.088 --> 00:23:45.716
GANGHA 3-DONG ABANDONED HOUSE FIRE SCENE OF PAST HOMICIDE

00:23:49.678 --> 00:23:52.097
STILL DETERMINING THE CAUSE OF THE FIRE

00:24:16.872 --> 00:24:17.956
Fingerprints.

00:25:03.627 --> 00:25:04.712
:cue

00:25:16.015 --> 00:25:17.683
Looks like a burner phone.

00:25:23.564 --> 00:25:25.023
Hey.

00:25:25.024 --> 00:25:27.483
We got a new job. Where are you?

00:25:28.652 --> 00:25:29.653
The reservoir?

00:25:30.487 --> 00:25:32.865
You still haven't taken care of that?

00:25:33.657 --> 00:25:35.992
Someone set fire to our burial site.

00:25:35.993 --> 00:25:37.286
What are you talking about?

00:25:37.870 --> 00:25:39.163
There were cops there.

00:25:40.330 --> 00:25:41.915
Those useless morons.

00:25:43.208 --> 00:25:45.085
They got scared and couldn't kill them.

00:25:46.587 --> 00:25:48.337
They just tied them up and bailed.

00:25:48.338 --> 00:25:49.339
But then,

00:25:51.091 --> 00:25:52.842
Looks like someone set it on fire.

00:25:52.843 --> 00:25:56.429
Wait, so do we make a run for it?

00:25:56.430 --> 00:25:57.639
Why? They found nothing.

00:25:58.390 --> 00:25:59.640
Who's the client?

00:25:59.641 --> 00:26:00.684
I don't know.

00:26:01.351 --> 00:26:04.104
Some kind of drug cartel. He wants me to find someone.

00:26:07.066 --> 00:26:08.191
What's his name?

00:26:08.192 --> 00:26:09.442
I don't know that either.

00:26:09.443 --> 00:26:11.028
If I don't find him in three days,

00:26:12.237 --> 00:26:13.947
He said he'll set this place on fire.

00:26:36.720 --> 00:26:38.013
He's a cop.

00:26:39.890 --> 00:26:40.973
A cop?

00:26:48.232 --> 00:26:50.858
They must've found the bodies at our burial site.

00:26:50.859 --> 00:26:52.860
Then what do we do?

00:26:52.861 --> 00:26:53.904
Don't be scared.

00:26:54.613 --> 00:26:56.614
They won't find any evidence.

00:26:56.615 --> 00:26:59.159
But what about me? What do I do?

00:27:01.620 --> 00:27:03.622
Burn all the records and go off the grid.

00:27:29.690 --> 00:27:30.732
Your phones.

00:28:00.971 --> 00:28:02.306
We're flying out at dawn.

00:28:04.141 --> 00:28:05.350
Let's go on vacation.

00:28:06.351 --> 00:28:07.352
Where do you wanna go?

00:28:17.738 --> 00:28:20.406
- Hey, get all the files out. - What?

00:28:20.407 --> 00:28:22.659
Get all the files out, right now!

00:28:23.327 --> 00:28:24.369
Yes, okay.

00:28:33.754 --> 00:28:35.088
Freeze.

00:28:37.257 --> 00:28:38.341
Damn it.

00:28:39.718 --> 00:28:41.178
:cue

00:28:57.361 --> 00:28:58.778
The reservoir?

00:28:58.779 --> 00:29:01.280
You still haven't taken care of that?

00:29:01.281 --> 00:29:02.949
Where's this reservoir?

00:29:02.950 --> 00:29:06.744
This is illegal wiretapping!

00:29:06.745 --> 00:29:10.623
This won't hold up as evidence in court anyway.

00:29:10.624 --> 00:29:11.958
You know that! Right?

00:29:11.959 --> 00:29:14.251
You sure we won't find any evidence over there?

00:29:14.252 --> 00:29:15.837
I doubt it.

00:29:18.382 --> 00:29:20.008
Right now,

00:29:20.717 --> 00:29:22.803
I'm in a real bad mood because you played me.

00:29:24.304 --> 00:29:25.805
While we investigate that,

00:29:25.806 --> 00:29:28.100
The real killers will get away.

00:29:29.643 --> 00:29:31.519
Then you'll become the main culprit.

00:29:31.520 --> 00:29:34.773
No, but... You have no evidence!

00:29:37.526 --> 00:29:39.111
Let's see the evidence.

00:29:47.661 --> 00:29:49.162
- What's your name? - What?

00:29:50.372 --> 00:29:51.498
Your name.

00:29:52.457 --> 00:29:53.958
Lee Eunjeong.

00:29:53.959 --> 00:29:55.918
Right, Eunjeong.

00:29:55.919 --> 00:29:56.920
Got a boyfriend?

00:29:57.921 --> 00:30:00.297
Yes, we're planning to get married.

00:30:00.298 --> 00:30:01.382
That's a shame.

00:30:01.383 --> 00:30:02.466
Congratulations.

00:30:02.467 --> 00:30:05.262
But will he wait a decade for you?

00:30:06.221 --> 00:30:08.347
- What? - This is a hitman's office.

00:30:08.348 --> 00:30:10.516
Over five people have been killed already.

00:30:10.517 --> 00:30:14.103
Even if you're just a minor accomplice, you'd get at least 10 years. Right?

00:30:14.104 --> 00:30:15.813
- Of course. - For sure.

00:30:15.814 --> 00:30:17.314
No, I...

00:30:17.315 --> 00:30:19.567
I don't know anything.

00:30:19.568 --> 00:30:21.820
I just took calls and made coffee.

00:30:22.779 --> 00:30:26.282
I don't know if the judge will believe that.

00:30:26.283 --> 00:30:28.368
Unless you help us catch the bad guys.

00:30:33.040 --> 00:30:35.541
Yeongil Reservoir. It's Yeongil Reservoir.

00:30:35.542 --> 00:30:37.293
I heard Mr. Myeong mention it once.

00:30:37.294 --> 00:30:39.045
- You idiot. - Sit down!

00:30:41.590 --> 00:30:43.050
They would've bolted by now.

00:30:43.759 --> 00:30:45.843
- I'll go check it out. - Got it.

00:30:45.844 --> 00:30:47.179
-  Let's go. -  Yes, sir.

00:30:48.930 --> 00:30:50.724
You must be in shock. Here, drink this.

00:30:52.893 --> 00:30:54.727
Can I go home now?

00:30:54.728 --> 00:30:56.687
Of course not. We have to question you.

00:30:56.688 --> 00:30:57.772
What?

00:30:57.773 --> 00:31:00.733
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

00:31:00.734 --> 00:31:03.319
Gwangjin-gu, Seoul. Lee Eunjeong.

00:31:03.320 --> 00:31:04.653
You're Korean, right?

00:31:04.654 --> 00:31:05.906
I don't know.

00:31:06.865 --> 00:31:08.283
You don't know?

00:31:08.992 --> 00:31:10.951
You know the victim, Kim Minseo, right?

00:31:10.952 --> 00:31:13.580
I don't know. I really don't know her.

00:31:16.291 --> 00:31:19.544
You ordered Lee Kyungsu to tail Ms. Kim Minseo, didn't you?

00:31:26.176 --> 00:31:29.845
Come on, stop saying you don't know. You and that dopey PI...

00:31:29.846 --> 00:31:31.598
I really don't know.

00:31:32.682 --> 00:31:35.268
Oh, my God, I want to go home.

00:32:01.962 --> 00:32:03.463
They torched the whole thing.

00:32:06.383 --> 00:32:07.843
There's a suitcase in the trunk.

00:32:32.159 --> 00:32:33.160
It's that car.

00:32:33.743 --> 00:32:35.202
Please keep tracking them.

00:32:35.203 --> 00:32:36.204
Got it. :cue

00:32:56.933 --> 00:32:57.934
There's nothing.

00:32:59.811 --> 00:33:00.854
I need the blue light.

00:33:28.632 --> 00:33:29.674
Detective Joo.

00:33:32.719 --> 00:33:33.845
We got a fingerprint.

00:33:34.804 --> 00:33:36.765
SCANNING

00:33:46.149 --> 00:33:47.733
Jang Jaechun.

00:33:47.734 --> 00:33:49.652
JANG JAECHUN

00:33:49.653 --> 00:33:51.528
"Seongju State Prison."

00:33:51.529 --> 00:33:52.906
Seongju State Prison?

00:33:59.246 --> 00:34:00.537
2019 SEONGJU STATE PRISON

00:34:00.538 --> 00:34:02.958
He was in the same prison as Myeong Seokho.

00:34:04.334 --> 00:34:05.751
Let's look into Jang Jaechun.

00:34:05.752 --> 00:34:07.503
I'll contact the prison.

00:34:07.504 --> 00:34:08.755
I'll look into his family.

00:34:25.605 --> 00:34:27.731
A phone was found at the reservoir.

00:34:27.732 --> 00:34:29.192
We got a fingerprint, too.

00:34:32.988 --> 00:34:35.156
You have an accomplice. Who is it?

00:34:39.327 --> 00:34:40.912
Forensics will recover everything.

00:34:44.958 --> 00:34:47.127
You know how a trial works.

00:34:47.585 --> 00:34:51.131
Cooperating with the investigation and showing signs of remorse

00:34:51.798 --> 00:34:53.800
Are important considerations in court.

00:34:54.592 --> 00:34:56.136
You're out of options now.

00:34:56.803 --> 00:34:59.264
Wouldn't it be smarter to try and reduce your sentence?

00:35:04.978 --> 00:35:05.979
So...

00:35:07.939 --> 00:35:09.441
His name's Jo Beomki.

00:35:10.150 --> 00:35:12.151
He's Jaechun's old classmate.

00:35:12.152 --> 00:35:14.653
But all I did was make the introduction.

00:35:14.654 --> 00:35:16.405
They asked me for work.

00:35:16.406 --> 00:35:19.367
How was I supposed to know they'd kill someone? I had no idea.

00:35:20.827 --> 00:35:21.911
Where are they?

00:35:23.997 --> 00:35:25.749
I really don't know.

00:35:33.506 --> 00:35:34.674
Did you find anything?

00:35:35.383 --> 00:35:36.426
No.

00:35:37.385 --> 00:35:38.844
Nothing much.

00:35:38.845 --> 00:35:40.722
Myeong Seokho named his accomplice.

00:35:50.148 --> 00:35:51.358
JO BEOMKI

00:35:51.983 --> 00:35:53.193
Where are they?

00:35:53.943 --> 00:35:54.944
He doesn't know.

00:36:11.044 --> 00:36:13.838
Find out where Jang Jaechun and Jo Beomki are.

00:36:14.881 --> 00:36:18.343
If making introductions was really all you did,

00:36:19.469 --> 00:36:21.221
You shouldn't go down with them. :cue

00:36:57.132 --> 00:36:59.550
Granny.

00:36:59.551 --> 00:37:02.052
I told you to just go to bed.

00:37:02.053 --> 00:37:04.638
How can I go to bed when your friends are here?

00:37:04.639 --> 00:37:07.517
- Want me to cook something? - Nah, just go to sleep already.

00:37:09.102 --> 00:37:10.185
Help yourself.

00:37:10.186 --> 00:37:12.312
Yes, thank you. What's this? Kimchi?

00:37:12.313 --> 00:37:15.315
-  Thank you, Granny. Good night. -  Night.

00:37:15.316 --> 00:37:17.776
I wish you a long and healthy life.

00:37:26.828 --> 00:37:29.371
INCOMING CALL

00:37:52.187 --> 00:37:53.188
Hey.

00:37:54.898 --> 00:37:56.274
Where are you?

00:37:59.277 --> 00:38:01.613
Somewhere safe. Why? Where are you?

00:38:02.530 --> 00:38:06.283
I just checked into a random motel.

00:38:06.284 --> 00:38:07.868
Then just hole up in there.

00:38:07.869 --> 00:38:09.578
We're getting out of here tomorrow.

00:38:09.579 --> 00:38:10.662
Where are you going?

00:38:10.663 --> 00:38:11.998
Why do you want to know?

00:38:12.624 --> 00:38:14.833
Hey, take me with you.

00:38:14.834 --> 00:38:15.919
Don't be ridiculous.

00:38:16.586 --> 00:38:18.420
I'm freaking out here.

00:38:18.421 --> 00:38:20.255
Why are you acting like a moron?

00:38:20.256 --> 00:38:22.842
Just lay low for a while, then make your move. Got it?

00:38:23.468 --> 00:38:25.011
Hey, Beomki!

00:38:28.765 --> 00:38:31.391
You bastard. You two are the ones who killed someone.

00:38:31.392 --> 00:38:33.061
What are you going to do about this?

00:38:38.441 --> 00:38:40.568
We're flying out of Busan first thing tomorrow.

00:38:41.486 --> 00:38:42.821
I'll call you once I'm there.

00:39:13.977 --> 00:39:14.978
What is it?

00:39:17.897 --> 00:39:19.022
It's just...

00:39:19.023 --> 00:39:20.942
We don't know where they're headed,

00:39:21.526 --> 00:39:23.694
And catching someone at an airport isn't easy.

00:39:23.695 --> 00:39:26.071
They're ruthless killers, so if we're not careful,

00:39:26.072 --> 00:39:27.364
Civilians could get hurt.

00:39:27.365 --> 00:39:30.409
We won't be able to stop them at the entrance.

00:39:30.410 --> 00:39:31.744
It'll have to be at security.

00:39:32.662 --> 00:39:34.872
- Notify the airport first. - Got it.

00:39:34.873 --> 00:39:36.624
- I'll report to the chief. -  Okay. :cue

00:39:38.334 --> 00:39:40.044
I got their location.

00:39:41.421 --> 00:39:44.674
I got them as far as Wonsan-eup in Daegu, but nothing after that.

00:39:45.341 --> 00:39:46.885
Wonsan-eup, Daegu?

00:39:50.471 --> 00:39:52.431
FAMILY RECORDS JANG JAECHUN

00:39:52.432 --> 00:39:54.016
Wonsan-eup, Daegu.

00:39:54.017 --> 00:39:55.809
Jang's grandma lives there.

00:40:03.651 --> 00:40:05.445
SATELLITE MAP SEARCH

00:40:08.823 --> 00:40:10.325
4-26 DURE-GIL, WONSAN-EUP, DAEGU

00:40:10.950 --> 00:40:12.869
That's right. I got them as far as here.

00:40:14.329 --> 00:40:15.996
Let's go catch them now.

00:40:20.001 --> 00:40:21.002
Let's go!

00:40:22.170 --> 00:40:23.171
Move out.

00:40:32.221 --> 00:40:34.223
- It'll take 3 hours and 20 minutes. - Huh?

00:40:36.976 --> 00:40:38.102
Hold on.

00:40:42.982 --> 00:40:44.192
That's way too long.

00:40:45.109 --> 00:40:47.695
These guys are smart. What if they catch on and bolt?

00:40:49.197 --> 00:40:50.406
Then what else can we do?

00:41:13.805 --> 00:41:15.180
Yes, Detective Jin.

00:41:15.181 --> 00:41:17.224
Mr. Choi, where are you?

00:41:17.225 --> 00:41:18.809
I'm in the helicopter.

00:41:18.810 --> 00:41:20.435
I was in Ulsan until now.

00:41:20.436 --> 00:41:21.812
No way.

00:41:21.813 --> 00:41:24.439
I need the chopper. Bring it to the station.

00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:25.524
What?

00:41:25.525 --> 00:41:27.234
I need to catch some hitmen.

00:41:27.235 --> 00:41:28.777
Please be quick.

00:41:35.243 --> 00:41:36.452
Turn the chopper around.

00:41:45.795 --> 00:41:47.213
I'll get a car here right away.

00:41:59.475 --> 00:42:00.560
Beomki!

00:42:02.895 --> 00:42:05.273
If we somehow get found out,

00:42:06.107 --> 00:42:08.775
Then we kill those two and the two of us just disappear.

00:42:08.776 --> 00:42:11.528
If I ever call you "Beomki,"

00:42:11.529 --> 00:42:12.739
That's the signal.

00:42:26.794 --> 00:42:27.962
:cue

00:42:56.491 --> 00:42:57.617
There it is.

00:43:02.830 --> 00:43:04.498
- Get ready. - Yes, ma'am.

00:43:04.499 --> 00:43:05.624
Yes, ma'am.

00:44:03.099 --> 00:44:04.517
Jaechun, is that you?

00:44:48.436 --> 00:44:49.770
What happened here?

00:45:07.663 --> 00:45:08.748
Detective Joo.

00:45:19.008 --> 00:45:20.091
Ma'am.

00:45:31.020 --> 00:45:32.270
Who are you?

00:45:37.151 --> 00:45:38.235
Stay with her.

00:45:38.236 --> 00:45:39.320
Got it.

00:45:43.032 --> 00:45:45.909
Ma'am, we're police officers.

00:45:45.910 --> 00:45:46.911
What?

00:45:47.787 --> 00:45:51.414
Why are you here? Did Jaechun do something bad again?

00:45:51.415 --> 00:45:52.458
Well...

00:45:56.921 --> 00:45:59.173
Yes, please send the forensics team.

00:45:59.799 --> 00:46:01.259
They're both dead.

00:46:02.718 --> 00:46:05.221
I need a patrol unit and an ambulance here.

00:46:05.846 --> 00:46:08.723
There's also an elderly lady here, and she's quite shaken up.

00:46:08.724 --> 00:46:10.642
We'll need backup.

00:46:10.643 --> 00:46:12.561
:cue

00:46:39.088 --> 00:46:40.381
They haven't been dead long.

00:46:41.048 --> 00:46:43.926
- Did they kill each other? - Why? They were planning to run.

00:46:48.222 --> 00:46:50.223
Did they get into a drunken fight?

00:46:50.224 --> 00:46:53.602
Killing the suspects to make it the perfect crime.

00:47:20.379 --> 00:47:22.214
There are three kinds of cigarettes.

00:47:26.427 --> 00:47:28.179
They haven't been dead long,

00:47:29.388 --> 00:47:30.556
So the perp's still here.

00:47:34.477 --> 00:47:36.561
Kyungjin, don't come outside.

00:47:39.023 --> 00:47:42.485
Oh. It's all right, ma'am. I'm sure it's nothing.

00:48:31.659 --> 00:48:32.785
The next one's live.

00:48:34.120 --> 00:48:37.581
Want to see who's faster, you or a bullet? Huh?

00:48:54.765 --> 00:48:56.349
Jin Isoo!

00:48:56.350 --> 00:48:57.351
Please.

00:49:12.241 --> 00:49:14.118
Hold still!

00:49:17.204 --> 00:49:19.873
I'm basically a sniper, right?

00:49:19.874 --> 00:49:21.625
You should've aimed a little higher.

00:49:22.251 --> 00:49:23.878
- Seriously? - Just kidding.

00:49:24.462 --> 00:49:25.463
Good shot.

00:49:26.338 --> 00:49:27.631
I taught you well.

00:49:28.382 --> 00:49:30.383
That's not what's important here.

00:49:30.384 --> 00:49:33.262
I'm basically John Wick.

00:49:36.765 --> 00:49:38.141
Hey, are you hurt?

00:49:38.142 --> 00:49:39.643
It's just a scratch.

00:49:44.773 --> 00:49:46.900
Hold still. It's to stop the bleeding.

00:49:46.901 --> 00:49:48.736
That really hurts.

00:49:59.622 --> 00:50:00.831
Oh...

00:50:01.415 --> 00:50:02.665
What's that?

00:50:02.666 --> 00:50:03.750
Pain medication.

00:50:03.751 --> 00:50:07.086
Don't give him that. He needs to suffer a bit more.

00:50:07.087 --> 00:50:09.297
Give it to me. I'm in a lot of pain.

00:50:10.716 --> 00:50:12.592
You asshole, you.

00:50:12.593 --> 00:50:14.053
How dare you throw chilis at me?

00:50:15.137 --> 00:50:17.181
Guess you couldn't outrun a bullet, huh?

00:50:18.098 --> 00:50:19.183
Asshole. :cue

00:50:23.938 --> 00:50:26.022
We've become a real married couple.

00:50:26.023 --> 00:50:28.650
That's what I think.

00:50:28.651 --> 00:50:31.110
What a lovey-dovey couple, huh?

00:50:31.111 --> 00:50:32.112
Nice weather.

00:50:32.821 --> 00:50:35.491
But what a shame. It's time to say goodbye.

00:50:36.242 --> 00:50:38.284
Oh, you even had a baby?

00:50:38.285 --> 00:50:39.828
Is it a boy, or a girl?

00:50:43.791 --> 00:50:44.792
It's a puppy.

00:50:45.376 --> 00:50:46.626
It was a puppy.

00:50:46.627 --> 00:50:47.710
Nam Jaeguk.

00:50:47.711 --> 00:50:50.922
You are hereby under arrest for soliciting the murder of Kim Minseo.

00:50:50.923 --> 00:50:54.300
You have the right to an attorney and the right to remain silent.

00:50:54.301 --> 00:50:56.427
You won't be penalized for remaining silent.

00:50:56.428 --> 00:50:58.221
- Got all that? - I was just...

00:50:58.222 --> 00:51:00.099
- I was taking a walk with my employee. - Honey.

00:51:01.225 --> 00:51:02.559
I was just...

00:51:02.560 --> 00:51:05.396
Did you really not know that your boyfriend killed his wife?

00:51:08.899 --> 00:51:10.859
You don't seem that oblivious.

00:51:12.111 --> 00:51:13.946
If you didn't know before, now you do.

00:51:15.155 --> 00:51:16.991
Someone died because of you.

00:51:20.035 --> 00:51:21.412
Mmm.

00:51:25.791 --> 00:51:27.167
Is it a crime to take a walk...

00:51:34.133 --> 00:51:35.383
Oh...

00:51:35.384 --> 00:51:37.135
You two haven't met before, right?

00:51:37.136 --> 00:51:39.095
Say hello. This is... No, this person.

00:51:39.096 --> 00:51:41.764
This is the scumbag who asked you to kill his wife.

00:51:41.765 --> 00:51:43.976
And this is the hitman who got the job.

00:51:44.935 --> 00:51:47.729
You should become friends. You'll be cellmates soon.

00:51:47.730 --> 00:51:49.105
Let's go.

00:51:49.106 --> 00:51:50.107
Yes, ma'am.

00:51:56.238 --> 00:51:58.324
They're here!

00:52:01.994 --> 00:52:02.995
Hurry up.

00:52:04.246 --> 00:52:05.580
Take his picture.

00:52:05.581 --> 00:52:06.957
Here.

00:52:17.509 --> 00:52:19.802
- Good job. Thanks. - Thank you for your hard work.

00:52:19.803 --> 00:52:21.847
- Hey, take them away. -  Yes, sir.

00:52:29.146 --> 00:52:30.147
Let's go.

00:52:35.152 --> 00:52:36.445
Heaven's on my side.

00:52:37.071 --> 00:52:38.906
Ah, another case closed.

00:52:44.161 --> 00:52:45.371
Please look this way!

00:52:47.915 --> 00:52:50.417
This way? Where? Like this?

00:52:51.001 --> 00:52:52.002
It's not over yet.

00:52:52.961 --> 00:52:54.045
Jin Isoo caught them.

00:52:54.046 --> 00:52:55.464
It was Jin Isoo.

00:52:57.549 --> 00:53:01.552
Now, let's walk through the case to find out what happened.

00:53:01.553 --> 00:53:03.763
Mr. Nam Jaeguk here

00:53:03.764 --> 00:53:07.475
Was suspicious of his wife and asked for an investigation into her movements.

00:53:07.476 --> 00:53:09.436
- Exactly. - And Mr. Dopey...

00:53:10.521 --> 00:53:14.440
Mr. Myeong Seokho here gave the job to Mr. Yu Taegwang.

00:53:14.441 --> 00:53:16.527
I only made the introduction.

00:53:18.028 --> 00:53:19.029
Sir.

00:53:20.364 --> 00:53:21.739
Then, Mr. Yu Taegwang,

00:53:21.740 --> 00:53:24.201
You committed a murder nobody hired you to commit.

00:53:25.786 --> 00:53:31.375
But how did you know that Mr. Nam Jaeguk wanted his wife dead?

00:53:32.042 --> 00:53:34.919
Are you psychic? Can you read minds?

00:53:34.920 --> 00:53:36.546
That's exactly it.

00:53:36.547 --> 00:53:38.256
I never asked them to kill her.

00:53:38.257 --> 00:53:42.219
For God's sake, why did you do something so stupid?

00:53:49.143 --> 00:53:50.436
You pieces of shit.

00:53:51.311 --> 00:53:54.313
- What the hell did you just... - I told you.

00:53:55.983 --> 00:53:57.818
If I go down, we all go down together.

00:53:59.987 --> 00:54:01.697
I recorded all the phone calls.

00:54:12.082 --> 00:54:13.500
He's called Nam Jaeguk. :cue

00:54:14.126 --> 00:54:15.294
He's having an affair.

00:54:16.378 --> 00:54:19.173
He wants us to kill his wife and make it look like a robbery.

00:54:19.882 --> 00:54:22.675
Game over, loser!

00:54:22.676 --> 00:54:25.345
-  This is a fake voice. - Get up.

00:54:26.180 --> 00:54:28.431
Don't be ridiculous, Mr. Dopey PI.

00:54:28.432 --> 00:54:30.517
This is AI-generated!

00:54:31.560 --> 00:54:34.146
Want to turn yourself in? You'll feel better afterward.

00:54:35.355 --> 00:54:37.273
It's not a crime to fall in love, right?

00:54:37.274 --> 00:54:38.775
I've been in love, too.

00:54:38.776 --> 00:54:41.111
It happens. We're only human.

00:54:50.245 --> 00:54:53.457
Write down the identities of the skeletal remains you buried.

00:54:56.376 --> 00:54:57.377
Skeletal remains?

00:54:59.713 --> 00:55:01.215
I'm not sure what you mean.

00:55:02.049 --> 00:55:05.469
Jang Jaechun and Jo Beomki were the ones who carried out the murders.

00:55:07.262 --> 00:55:09.515
But they killed each other,

00:55:10.724 --> 00:55:13.267
So your sentence won't be too harsh.

00:55:13.268 --> 00:55:15.102
You'll be better off if you cooperate.

00:55:46.051 --> 00:55:48.595
KIM JIHUN, OH SEA, HAN MINJAE

00:55:58.313 --> 00:56:00.148
Let me tell you something in return.

00:56:02.734 --> 00:56:04.861
That abandoned house you used as a burial site,

00:56:05.654 --> 00:56:08.282
There was a robbery and murder there 10 years ago.

00:56:12.869 --> 00:56:15.705
The killer's DNA was found at the scene,

00:56:15.706 --> 00:56:17.833
But there was no suspect to match it against.

00:56:18.792 --> 00:56:21.378
Why would you have used that place as a burial site?

00:56:24.089 --> 00:56:26.757
Is it possible that was your first murder?

00:56:26.758 --> 00:56:27.968
DNA ANALYSIS REPORT

00:56:29.344 --> 00:56:33.599
The DNA found at the abandoned house matched your DNA.

00:56:40.647 --> 00:56:42.399
Jo Beomki and Jang Jaechun.

00:56:43.483 --> 00:56:45.444
You killed them too, didn't you?

00:56:49.239 --> 00:56:51.283
And you washed the blood off in the bathroom.

00:57:00.626 --> 00:57:02.127
We found your fingerprint there.

00:57:06.882 --> 00:57:09.009
You thought you could play us, didn't you?

00:57:11.303 --> 00:57:12.512
The perfect crime?

00:57:13.805 --> 00:57:14.890
That doesn't exist.

00:57:29.988 --> 00:57:32.783
We're sorry for everything.

00:57:35.535 --> 00:57:36.620
The real culprit

00:57:38.121 --> 00:57:39.122
Has been arrested.

00:57:56.056 --> 00:57:58.015
"The brave citizen award."

00:57:58.016 --> 00:58:01.143
"Park Ahin, of Myeongun Middle School, Grade 9, Class 1."

00:58:01.144 --> 00:58:03.979
"In recognition of your unwavering support of

00:58:03.980 --> 00:58:06.607
And cooperation with law enforcement, :cue

00:58:06.608 --> 00:58:09.610
And for your assistance in the arrest of a dangerous criminal,

00:58:09.611 --> 00:58:10.986
We award this commendation."

00:58:10.987 --> 00:58:12.988
"February 10, 2025."

00:58:12.989 --> 00:58:15.826
"Gwon Taegyun, Chief of Police, Gangha Police Station."

00:58:16.368 --> 00:58:18.744
You're all here.

00:58:18.745 --> 00:58:20.956
- Congratulations, Ahin. - Thank you.

00:58:21.957 --> 00:58:23.416
This is a gift from me.

00:58:25.752 --> 00:58:29.130
It's the only one in the world. Custom-made in 24-karat gold.

00:58:29.131 --> 00:58:33.426
I'll study really hard and become a detective like you.

00:58:34.886 --> 00:58:36.096
That might be a challenge.

00:58:36.972 --> 00:58:39.391
The goal of a cool detective like me might be hard to reach.

00:58:39.975 --> 00:58:41.476
Aim for Detective Joo here.

00:58:43.478 --> 00:58:45.438
Here, let's meet again as colleagues.

00:58:45.439 --> 00:58:46.689
Okay.

00:58:46.690 --> 00:58:49.692
All right, back to work. I'm off.

00:58:49.693 --> 00:58:50.860
- Sir. -  What?

00:58:50.861 --> 00:58:53.154
- We've earned a vacation. - What do you mean?

00:58:53.155 --> 00:58:55.406
You were just doing your duty as detectives.

00:58:55.407 --> 00:58:57.074
Get your photos taken.

00:58:57.075 --> 00:59:00.454
We were doing our duty, but we still busted a murder ring.

00:59:47.584 --> 00:59:48.751
FLEX X COP 2 EPISODE 4

00:59:48.752 --> 00:59:50.252
CONCIERGE MANAGER OH MINYEONG

01:00:11.274 --> 01:00:14.777
Special Cast. Lee Hakju, Park Jungpyo, Kwon Seungwoo

01:00:14.778 --> 01:00:18.198
Special Cast. Park Soi

01:00:25.288 --> 01:00:27.289
Room 709 was unoccupied yesterday.

01:00:27.290 --> 01:00:29.542
That room has been vacant for two months.

01:00:29.543 --> 01:00:32.336
Why did she go to an unoccupied room alone?

01:00:32.337 --> 01:00:34.755
- Have you seen anyone suspicious lately? - The ugly guy?

01:00:34.756 --> 01:00:36.341
- Chunsik? - Isoo!

01:00:36.466 --> 01:00:38.301
I asked her out.

01:00:38.844 --> 01:00:40.886
The seventh floor camera isn't broken.

01:00:40.887 --> 01:00:42.096
I was following the CEO's orders.

01:00:42.097 --> 01:00:45.851
There was an assault here last Wednesday. He tried to drag her into Room 709?

01:00:46.935 --> 01:00:49.436
It did seem like she was seeing someone lately.

01:00:49.437 --> 01:00:50.980
I think it was one of the hotel staff.

01:00:50.981 --> 01:00:52.481
Are you going to keep interfering?

01:00:52.482 --> 01:00:54.483
What was he doing with the cameras off?

01:00:54.484 --> 01:00:56.235
I found something that looks like a bloodstain.

01:00:56.236 --> 01:00:58.445
Let's go. The suspect is on the seventh floor.

01:00:58.446 --> 01:01:00.406
Watch out! Step on it.

01:01:05.203 --> 01:01:06.204
Yes.

01:01:06.663 --> 01:01:08.039
I just arrived.

01:01:08.874 --> 01:01:09.875
Yes.

01:01:10.709 --> 01:01:11.834
I'll see you tomorrow.

01:01:23.263 --> 01:01:24.806
The chairman is waiting for you.

01:01:25.515 --> 01:01:27.975
I'll be leaving soon. I have no business with him.

01:01:27.976 --> 01:01:29.394
He ordered you to come home.

01:01:43.199 --> 01:01:44.576
Korea...

01:01:45.327 --> 01:01:48.038
Has too many security cameras.

01:01:51.625 --> 01:01:53.627
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

